{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_release_0_0_52", "label": "pkcore 0.0.52 Release Notes", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/RELEASE_0.0.52.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_release_0_0_52_heads_up_asymmetry_guard", "label": "Heads-Up Asymmetry Guard Dispatch Fix", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/RELEASE_0.0.52.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dispatching showdowns on active_in_hand().len()==2 was branching on the wrong dimension: what determines the correct payout algorithm is whether contributors committed equal amounts, not the player count. heads_up_is_symmetric() guards the fast path; asymmetric heads-up (mismatched all-ins, folded contributors) delegates to the side-pot-aware multiway path. Symmetric heads-up keeps the fast path and its PlayerWins event shape to minimize downstream breakage."}, {"id": "docs_release_0_0_52_tied_at_level_filter_bug", "label": "tied_at_level == vs >= Filter Bug", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/RELEASE_0.0.52.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The filter e.chips == winner_chip_level excluded tied winners whose remaining commitment was higher than the layer cap. Latent for the lifetime of both showdown implementations because TableEquity::new() consolidates equal-commitment winners into one row, accidentally making == correct; only mismatched-commitment ties (a shape no existing test exercised) exposed it. Fix: == changed to >= in Phase 1 (no-cell) and Phases 1 and 2 (cell)."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_release_0_0_52", "target": "docs_release_0_0_52_heads_up_asymmetry_guard", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/RELEASE_0.0.52.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"sour